    workDetails: "About CTeBS\n\nCTeBS (Classic Technologies & Business Solutions) is a purpose-built software company for the fashion manufacturing industry, and a subsidiary of Classic Fashion Apparel Industry Ltd. We build the Trendz Biz Suite — a unified enterprise platform covering production planning, ERP, quality management, HR, and data intelligence for fashion manufacturers.\n\nWith a 70+ person team in Kochi and live deployments in production, we are now scaling our engineering organisation to match our next phase of growth. This is a pivotal leadership hire.\n\nThe Role\n\nAs Head of Product Engineering, you will be CTeBS's senior-most engineering leader — building the leadership layer, establishing the culture, and designing the operating model that takes our engineering function from delivery-focused to capability-driven.\n\nYou will lead 30+ engineers across three product teams through a layer of Technical Managers, and sit on the CTeBS leadership team reporting directly to the Business Unit Head.\n\nThis is not a role for someone looking to grow into engineering leadership. It is for someone who has done it — and wants to do it again with full ownership and executive backing.\n\nWhat You Will Own\n\nEngineering Organisation & Culture\n\nLead three product engineering teams through Technical Managers — build their capability as much as the team's\n\nEstablish engineering values, norms, and a culture of accountability, ownership, and craft\n\nDesign and implement career ladders, performance frameworks, and individual development plans\n\nDrive active, structured hiring — own the talent pipeline from sourcing to onboarding\n\nStrategy & Delivery\n\nTranslate product vision and business goals into multi-quarter engineering plans\n\nMove the organisation from reactive firefighting to proactive, planned delivery\n\nOwn platform architecture direction in partnership with Solution Architecture\n\nRepresent engineering credibly at the leadership table — costs, timelines, tradeoffs\n\nTeam Building & Long-Term Thinking\n\nIdentify structural risks, capability gaps, and technical debt early — and build plans to address them\n\nCreate an environment where strong engineers stay, grow, and do their best work",
