    address: "Infopark, Kochi, Kerala",
    industry: "Infopark company",
    companyDetails: "2Base Technologies Pvt Ltd — listed on the official Infopark jobs portal.",
    workDetails: "2Base Technologies is at a deliberate stage of building its marketing content function, and this internship is the entry point into that function.\n\nWe are a technology services company with over 16 years of delivery experience, working with mid-market and enterprise clients across the United States and the United Kingdom. Our work spans custom software development, AI implementation, legacy system modernisation, and operational transformation.\n\nThis is an entry-level writing role with a specific, practical purpose. It is not a social media role and it is not a generalist marketing role. If that distinction is unclear from the outset, this is probably not the right fit.\n\nWhat This Role Exists to Do\n\nTechnology is complicated. Our job is to make it clear. This role exists to support the production of written content that explains what 2Base does, what problems we solve, and why that matters to the people we work with. The output is blog posts that earn attention, social copies that are actually read, and supporting content that helps the marketing function move.\n\nYou will work from structured briefs, receive direct feedback on every draft, and build a practical foundation in technology content writing. The audience is technical leaders and business decision-makers at mid-market companies. Writing that is clear, specific, and free of noise. That is the standard you will be working towards and learning to meet.\n\nWhat You Will Own\n\nFirst drafts of blog posts on technology topics including software development, AI implementation, digital transformation, and IT services written from structured briefs provided by the Marketing Manager\n\nSocial media copies for the 2Base LinkedIn page and other channels, produced to brief and reviewed before publishing\n\nResearch for content briefs – gathering background, understanding the topic, and returning with enough substance to write from\n\nSupporting long-form content production: contributing sections, drafts, and revisions under direction\n\nProofreading and editing your own drafts against 2Base brand voice guidelines before submitting\n\nWhat You Will Not Own",
