    workDetails: "We are seeking a detail-oriented Financial Analyst with 4–7 years of experience in Financial Analysis to support the Director – Finance in consolidating and presenting financial and business data for investor reporting and strengthening the organisation’s readiness for a future Initial Public Offering (IPO).\n\nThe role involves close coordination with Finance, Accounts, Legal, and business teams to prepare accurate, timely, and audit-ready financial models, MIS reports, data, and disclosures for existing and prospective investors and IPO due diligence.\n\nThe ideal candidate should have strong financial and analytical skills, excellent attention to detail, the ability to handle confidential information responsibly, and the discipline to meet tight reporting timelines.\n\nKey Responsibilities, Deliverables & Outcomes Investor Data Collation & Reporting:\n\nCollect, consolidate, and validate financial and operational data from various departments (Accounts, Sales, HR, Operations) to prepare periodic investor reports, board packs, and MIS dashboards for the Director – Finance.\n\nIPO Readiness Support: Assist in preparing and organising financial statements, schedules, disclosures, and supporting documentation required for IPO due diligence, in coordination with auditors, legal counsel, merchant bankers, and IPO consultants.\n\nData Room Management: Build, maintain, and continuously update a well-organised financial/legal data room for investor and IPO due diligence purposes, ensuring version control and confidentiality.\n\nFinancial Analysis & MIS: Prepare variance analysis, trend analysis, KPI trackers, and financial models/schedules to support investor queries and management decision-making.\n\nStakeholder Coordination: Liaise with internal stakeholders (Accounts, CEO Office, Global Leadership team) and external parties (auditors, bankers, consultants) to ensure timely and accurate data flow.\n\nCompliance & Governance: Ensure accuracy, consistency, and confidentiality across all investor and IPO-related documentation; support adherence to applicable listing/regulatory requirements.",
