    companyDetails: "Gravity Business Process Private Limited — listed on the official Infopark jobs portal.",
    workDetails: "System & Detailed Design\n\n•\tDesign complete industrial solutions, including fire and gas systems, control and monitoring systems, remote I/O, wireless instrumentation, communication gateways, power distribution, battery-backed, and solar-powered field systems.\n\n•\tDevelop system architecture, functional concepts, and practical technical solutions based on customer specifications, project scope, and applicable standards.\n\n•\tSelect suitable enclosures, instruments, controllers, I/O, power supplies, batteries, protection devices, terminals, cable glands, communication equipment, and accessories.\n\n•\tEnsure designs are suitable for production, installation, testing, operation, maintenance, and future modification.\n\nEngineering Drawings and Documentation:\n\n•\tPrepare cabinet and panel general arrangements, front views, internal arrangements, mounting-plate layouts, DIN-rail and cable-duct layouts, door layouts, and mechanical interface drawings.\n\n•\tDesign field cabinets, junction boxes, local control panels, field stations, supports, brackets, cable-entry arrangements, terminal layouts, gland layouts, antenna mounting, and instrument installation details.\n\n•\tPrepare electrical schematics, power and control diagrams, AC/DC distribution, battery, UPS and solar connections, grounding and bonding, relay logic, safety circuits, interconnection drawings, loop diagrams, I/O drawings, , RS485/Modbus and Industrial Network diagrams.\n\n•\tMaintain bills of materials, equipment lists, I/O lists, instrument indexes, cable and termination schedules, terminal plans, load lists, calculations, document registers, manufacturing drawings, and as-built documentation.\n\nProject Planning and Coordination:\n\n•\tPlan assigned engineering activities, estimate hours, define deliverables and milestones, maintain drawing and document registers, and report progress, risks, and technical issues.\n\n•\tCoordinate technical inputs and clarifications with customers, suppliers, subcontractors, procurement, production, testing, and other engineering disciplines.",
