    website: "https://www.whiterabbit.group",
    address: "Infopark, Kochi, Kerala",
    industry: "Infopark company",
    companyDetails: "White Rabbit Group — listed on the official Infopark jobs portal.",
    workDetails: "Experience : 3+ Years | Work Location : Kochi (hybrid)\n\n𝗪𝗵𝗮𝘁 𝘄𝗲'𝗿𝗲 𝗹𝗼𝗼𝗸𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗳𝗼𝗿\n\nYou might know 𝗔𝗹𝗹𝘆 from our roots at 𝗪𝗵𝗶𝘁𝗲 𝗥𝗮𝗯𝗯𝗶𝘁 𝗚𝗿𝗼𝘂𝗽. At Ally, we’re on a mission to bridge the gap between legal compliance and true digital inclusion by making compliance simple and accessibility personal.\n\nAlly is seeking a passionate 𝗔𝗰𝗰𝗲𝘀𝘀𝗶𝗯𝗶𝗹𝗶𝘁𝘆 𝗤𝗔 𝗘𝗻𝗴𝗶𝗻𝗲𝗲𝗿 who is committed to creating inclusive digital experiences. You will help champion a Shift Left accessibility culture by ensuring accessibility is embedded throughout design, development, and quality assurance. This role combines expert manual accessibility testing, automated validation, and traditional QA to deliver exceptional digital experiences that meet the highest accessibility standards.\n\nAt Ally, we believe accessibility experts have a responsibility to raise the standard of our industry. We invest heavily in training, certifications, and continuous learning, and every team member is expected to continuously grow as an accessibility expert.\n\n𝗥𝗲𝘀𝗽𝗼𝗻𝘀𝗶𝗯𝗶𝗹𝗶𝘁𝗶𝗲𝘀\n\n* Create and execute accessibility test plans and test cases for web and mobile applications.\n\n* Perform comprehensive manual accessibility testing using assistive technologies including NVDA, JAWS, VoiceOver, TalkBack, keyboard-only navigation, screen magnification, and other adaptive technologies.\n\n* Perform automated accessibility validation using tools such as Axe-core, Pa11y, WAVE, Lighthouse, and Accessibility Insights.\n\n* Validate accessibility against WCAG 2.2 AA and client-specific compliance requirements.\n\n* Review design files and developer implementations for accessibility throughout the development lifecycle.\n\n* Document accessibility issues with clear reproduction steps, root-cause analysis, and remediation recommendations.\n\n* Contribute to the creation of high-quality VPATs and Accessibility Conformance Reports (ACRs).\n\n* Plan and execute functional, usability, regression, cross-browser, and responsive testing.\n\n* Create and review test plans and test cases.\n\n* Collaborate closely with Designers, Developers, and Project Managers to integrate accessibility throughout the SDLC.",
